// Example parameters for infra/azure/main.bicep.
//
// COPY to main.bicepparam and fill in real values BEFORE any deploy. This file
// is the committed, secret-free template — main.bicepparam is gitignored.
// There are NO secrets here: Redis keys, App Insights connection strings, and
// ACR credentials are all resolved at deploy time inside the template via
// listKeys()/managed identity, never passed as parameters.
//
// Reference IaC only — this stack is NOT deployed ($0). See infra/azure/README.md.

using './main.bicep'

param environmentName = 'dev'
param baseName = 'arp'

// Point at the image your ACR builds (e.g. '<acr>.azurecr.io/arp:<gitsha>').
// Left as the public quickstart image so `az bicep build` has a valid default.
param containerImage = 'mcr.microsoft.com/k8se/quickstart:latest'

// Horizontal-scale envelope — minReplicas >= 2 mirrors the multi-replica
// Redis-CAS proof (at least two replicas sharing one Redis under load).
param minReplicas = 2
param maxReplicas = 10
param concurrentRequestsPerReplica = 50

param cpuCores = '0.5'
param memorySize = '1.0Gi'
